Subject: [PATCH 08/11] feat(pqc-m8): wrap-key health check + CLI alias helpers

PQC migration (whitepaper 2.2.7 + 2.2.8): the health-check surface
that surfaces Doctor guidance, plus thin CLI-alias helpers for the
future `openclaw wrap-key status|export|import` commands. The
actual CLI registration is left for a later milestone; the aliases
land on the same shared helpers so the registration step is a
mechanical wire-up.

- src/security/wrap-key-cli.ts:
  - wrapKeyHealthCheck returns a JSON-friendly status document
    classifying each device-identity row as plaintext,
    wrapped-active, wrapped-stale, or invalid. Notes are emitted
    in priority order (invalid > stale > plaintext) so the CLI
    surfaces the most urgent guidance first.
  - parseWrapEnvelope is a defensive probe: it returns null for
    any malformed input and never throws, so the health check can
    keep reporting on the remaining rows.
  - wrapKeyStatusCommand / wrapKeyExportCommand /
    wrapKeyImportCommand are the documented entry aliases; the
    export/import ones delegate to M7's exportWrapKey /
    importWrapKey to keep a single canonical implementation.
- src/security/wrap-key-cli.test.ts: 12 invariants - the four
  status branches, missing-keyring / null-activeKeyId treatment,
  defensive parseWrapEnvelope (null / empty / bad base64 / bad
  JSON), CLI-alias equality, export+import round-trip, wrong-
  passphrase rejection, throw on missing list, and the
  priority-ordered notes contract.

